# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# HARDENING: a MISSING /assets/* must return 404 — NOT the SPA fallback (200
# index.html). Without this, the project's single-page not_found_handling serves
# index.html (text/html, 200) for any not-yet-present hashed chunk. During a
# deploy-propagation race that 200 text/html gets cached under the asset URL and
# frozen by the `immutable` Cache-Control in _headers, so browsers receive HTML
# for a JS module → "Expected a JavaScript module … MIME type text/html" → the
# app never mounts. A 404 can't masquerade as a module and isn't cached as an
# immutable success, so the poisoning can't recur. Real assets are static-matched
# and served before this rule ever applies.
/assets/*  /404.html  404
